# cert-manager DNS-01 solver webhook for Gandi — public profile, gated on
# components.dns01-gandi. Pairs with the dns01-gandi release, which creates the
# letsencrypt-prod ClusterIssuer that dispatches to this webhook.
#
# The webhook is not a controller: it registers as an aggregated APIService under
# `groupName` and cert-manager calls it synchronously to write/delete the
# _acme-challenge TXT record. It is idle between renewals.
#
# The PAT arrives as an env var rather than a *.secret.yaml overlay so following
# the guide is one file (`cp .env.example .env`) rather than two. The chart turns
# this value into the `gandi-credentials` Secret in the cert-manager namespace —
# which is where a ClusterIssuer resolves its secrets, NOT the namespace of the
# Certificate that used it. requiredEnv, not env: a chart that renders with an
# empty PAT deploys a webhook that fails every challenge with a 401.
gandiPat: {{ requiredEnv "DPL_GANDI_PAT" | quote }}
